.TH HOARD-GUI 1 "August 2026" "hoard 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hoard-gui \- a window for the hoard vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hoard-gui
.RI [ VAULT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hoard-gui
opens a GTK window onto the vault managed by
.BR hoard (1).
It prompts for the master password, then lists the entries and lets you copy,
add, edit and remove them.
.PP
Every cryptographic operation is performed by the
.B hoard
module. Nothing in the window derives a key, chooses a nonce or touches a
cipher, so there is one implementation of the vault format rather than two that
have to be kept in agreement.
.PP
The window deliberately follows the system GTK theme instead of shipping its own
colours, so it looks like the rest of the desktop rather than like a brand. The
only override is that secrets are shown in a monospace font, so that l, 1 and I,
and 0 and O, cannot be confused when read aloud or copied by hand.
.PP
The vault locks itself again after five minutes without interaction.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I VAULT
Path to the vault. Defaults to the same location
.BR hoard (1)
uses.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The window can export a diagnostic report for bug reports. It redacts entry
names and never includes passwords.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.hoard/vault
The vault.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOARD_VAULT
Path to the vault, overriding the default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hoard (1)
.SH AUTHOR
konnen916
